# Until 2026-09-04 this file was a SYMLINK to legacy-eoreader6.1/.gitignore.
# Git could not resolve it — every command printed
#   warning: unable to access '.gitignore': Too many levels of symbolic links
# — and so honored NO ignore rules at all, not even node_modules/. That is
# why regenerable eval output accumulated in the tree. It is a real file now.

node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Regenerable eval output. Neither of these is read by the test suite —
# checked, not assumed: `npm test` and `npm run test:organs` reference only
# ddg-*.html, midi/, pos-prior-eng.json, unimorph-morphology-prior.json,
# wikipedia-war-and-peace.html, wikipedia-apollo-11.html and
# wikipedia-battle-of-austerlitz.html, all of which stay tracked so the
# suite keeps running with no network.
#
# primary-faces is ranke-backwards.mjs's offline replay cache of fetched
# third-party documents (archive.org captures, Google Books, LoC records);
# the results JSON are run outputs. The results/*.md write-ups are the
# findings themselves and are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Files already committed stay tracked — an ignore rule does not untrack
# anything. This stops NEW cache from landing; it does not remove the
# ~5.7 MB already on main.
native/eval/the-fold/fixtures/primary-faces/
native/eval/the-fold/results/*.json
native/eval/results/*.json
native/eval/lavar/results/*-test.json
native/eval/the-fold/results/longform-multi-type-*/
native/eval/the-fold/results/longform-code-*/

# Fetched third-party PAGES cached for offline replay — the same category as
# primary-faces above, extended 2026-09-04 when a 512 KB news page landed in a
# branch. The AGENCY RECORDS beside them stay tracked (usgs-*.json, isc.csv,
# emsc.json, 71 KB together): those are the measured oracle a falsifiable run
# is scored against, not a cache of prose, and sanriku-quantities.mjs already
# degrades with a named "(absent: …)" line when a page is missing.
native/eval/the-fold/fixtures/sanriku/*.html

# The Chicago world's fair corpus, relocated out of the repo root on
# 2026-09-15 (Kondo sweep): retained third-party web pages read by
# demo-void-outline.mjs and vonnegut-extract.mjs — the same fetched-pages-
# kept-local category as sanriku and primary-faces above, never committed.
native/eval/the-fold/fixtures/chicago/

# Python bytecode caches from the visual-detect helper beside it.
native/eval/lavar/__pycache__/

# civic-research-walk.mjs (and any subject-naming investigative walk this
# driver shape is reused for) is a TEST OF THE INSTRUMENT, not a permanent
# finding, and its target is frequently a real, specific, living subject —
# unlike sanriku's earthquake catalog or primary-faces' public-domain
# archive captures above. Neither the fetched pages nor the produced
# reading is kept: the CODE (the driver, the organs, their tests) is the
# artifact this repo owns; the material a run reads and the document it
# writes are the run's own, regenerable by re-running it, and belong beside
# wherever that run's subject material is held — never committed here.
native/eval/the-fold/fixtures/research-faces/
native/eval/the-fold/results/civic-research-READING.md
native/eval/the-fold/results/*-READING.md

# conversation-eval run outputs (2026-09-07): the ledger on disk, the
# constitutional reading on disk (80 MB for one novel), and each run's
# turns.jsonl are reproduced from the corpus + recipe by
# native/eval/the-fold/conversation.mjs. The results/*.md write-ups and
# the lib/ computations a test reads are what is kept.
native/eval/the-fold/results/readings/
native/eval/the-fold/results/ledgers/
native/eval/the-fold/results/conversation/

# EOReader7 proxy runtime
proxy.log
.er7-proxy.pid
test run/
documents/
heimdall-log.jsonl
native/the-fold/speaker-models/*.json
_dbg_*.mjs
_diag_*.mjs
_smoke_*.mjs
cli/alice.txt
proxy-debug.mjs
*.bak
